# Design Themes — Document Brand Tokens (Permanent)

## Law

**Two different “themes” — never conflate them.**

| Concern | Store | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **App chrome** (dark / light) | Cookie `vdb-theme`, CSS variables in Next | Product UI only — see `10-theme-and-i18n.mdc` |
| **Document brand** (`design_themes`) | PostgreSQL per Business | Colors / typography / font refs for **documents, templates, PDF** |

Do not put document brand colors in the app chrome cookie. Do not use Mongo for theme tokens unless an ADR says otherwise.

## Data model

- Table `design_themes`: `business_id`, `name`, `is_default`, `tokens` (JSONB), timestamps, optional soft-delete.
- Every Business gets **at least one default** theme (seed on Business create; `ensureDefault` if missing).
- Tokens live in PostgreSQL JSONB — validated against shared-types shape.

## Token contract (MVP)

Stable keys in `packages/shared-types` (`DesignThemeTokens`):

- `colors.primary` | `secondary` | `text` | `background` (hex `#RRGGBB` or `#RGB`)
- `typography.headingFamily` | `bodyFamily` | weights | `baseSizePx`
- `fonts.headingFontFaceId` | `bodyFontFaceId` — optional FKs to `font_faces.id` (same `businessId`); null = CSS family name only

Unknown keys may be rejected or stripped on write — prefer strict validation.

## API / gates

- Routes under `/api/businesses/:businessId/themes`
- List / get: membership
- Create / patch / delete / set-default: `EntitlementGuard` + `@RequireWritable`
- Resolve font face ids against `font_faces` filtered by `businessId` + `deletedAt IS NULL`

## Consumers

- Theme picker UI, Template/Document editor, PDF renderer resolve tokens → CSS / embed fonts.
- Preview in settings is HTML/CSS only — not a PDF render.
